TEXT 1040 784 Left 1 ;T-Motor MN601-S (KV320)\nfirmware ID 2026-09-27:\nR 98 mOhm, Ld 7.9 uH, Lq 11.0 uH\nstandstill -> no back-EMF
TEXT 1392 88 Left 1 ;CSA A: SPA = SRC_A, SNA = GND (Kelvin)   settling   SOx pin    -> MCU ADC (TP17)
TEXT 1392 440 Left 1 ;CSA B: SPB = SRC_B, SNB = GND (Kelvin)   settling   SOx pin    -> MCU ADC (TP16)
TEXT 1376 720 Left 1 ;DRV8323 CSA: SOx = VREF/2 - G x (SPx - SNx).  Positive phase current (out of the leg) flows UP\nthrough the low-side shunt, so SOx rises above VREF/2 (matches the firmware sign, APP_CSA_SIGN_A = +1).
TEXT -1392 368 Left 1 ;MCU (TIM1 centre-aligned, 25 kHz, 200 ns dead time) + PI current loop on alpha, like RUN ID_R.\nHS on while duty > carrier; LS on around the carrier peak, where the ADC samples.
TEXT -1000 -600 Left 3 ;03b BENCH VARIANT - 0.8 A along +alpha (RUN ID_R first step), 12 V (phase A +5 A, B and C -2.5 A each), 30 V, 25 kHz centre-aligned
TEXT -1000 -552 Left 1 ;Question: at the firmware's ID_R / hold operating point, what phase-current ripple does the MN601-S's low inductance give, what does the CSA output look like\non the scope, and has it settled when the ADC samples at the carrier peak?  This is also the scale/offset check: I_from_CSA vs the true winding current.\nPASS: IA_avg within 2 % of Iset; CSA-derived current within 2 % of the true current at the sample instant; SOA flat at VREF/2 while the high side conducts.\nBench (RUN ID_R or a HOLD at Iset, MN601-S clamped): DHO804 CH1 on SOA (TP20) or FILTER_SOA (TP17), CH2 on PWM_PHASEA_L (TP22) as the trigger, CH3 on SW_A.\nBM235 in series with the supply (10 A range) or the KA3005P display: compare with Isup_avg.  Firmware GUI current reading: compare with IA_csa.
TEXT 1440 -520 Left 1 ;HOW TO EDIT (.param lines below)\n  Vbus             bus voltage, V                       (30)\n  Iset             held current along +alpha, A         (5; phase A carries Iset, B and C -Iset/2)\n  R_meas           phase resistance from firmware ID_R  (98 mOhm; matches the DC line-line 195 mOhm,\n                   so it is motor + leads; the FETs and shunts are modelled separately)\n  Ld, Lq           firmware ID_L, H                     (7.9 / 11.0 uH; the sim uses the mean, as the firmware)\n  lambda, pp, J    flux linkage 1.389 mV.s, 14 pole pairs, 8e-5 kg.m2: not used at standstill,\n                   listed so all firmware motor constants live on one sheet\n  fsw, DT          25 kHz, 200 ns                       (APP_PWM_FREQ_HZ, TIM1 DTG=34)\n  G, VREF, tSET    CSA gain 20 (p_csa_gain), 3.3 V, 600 ns settling to 1 % at G=20 (datasheet)\n  fc               PI current-loop crossover in this model only (the firmware loop is digital)
TEXT -1000 1120 Left 2 !.include ../../lib/ISC030N10NM6_fit.lib\n.param Vbus=12 Iset=0.8 fsw=25k DT=200n\n.param R_meas=98m Ld=7.9u Lq=11.0u lambda=1.389m pp=14 J=8e-5\n.param Rph=R_meas Lph={(Ld+Lq)/2}\n.param Rsh=3m G=20 VREF=3.3 tSET=600n\n.param Isrc=1.0 Isnk=2.0 Vgsh=11 Vgsl=11\n.param fc=1k Kp={2*pi*fc*1.5*Lph/Vbus} Ki={Kp*Rph/Lph}\n.param u0={(1.5*(Rph+4m)*Iset+2*Vbus*DT*fsw)/Vbus}   ; feed-forward start (R drop + dead-time loss)\n.ic I(LA)={Iset} I(LB)={-Iset/2} I(LC)={-Iset/2}\n.param ts={24.5/fsw}   ; ADC sample instant = carrier peak (centre of the low-side window)\n.tran 0 1m 0 2n\n.options plotwinsize=0
TEXT -160 1120 Left 2 !.meas TRAN IA_avg AVG I(LA) FROM {21/fsw} TO {25/fsw}\n.meas TRAN IA_pp PP I(LA) FROM {23/fsw} TO {25/fsw}\n.meas TRAN IB_avg AVG I(LB) FROM {21/fsw} TO {25/fsw}\n.meas TRAN IA_true FIND I(LA) AT ts\n.meas TRAN SOA_s FIND V(FILTER_SOA) AT ts\n.meas TRAN IA_csa PARAM (SOA_s-VREF/2)/(G*Rsh)\n.meas TRAN IA_err_pct PARAM (IA_csa-IA_true)/IA_true*100\n.meas TRAN IB_true FIND I(LB) AT ts\n.meas TRAN SOB_s FIND V(FILTER_SOB) AT ts\n.meas TRAN IB_csa PARAM (SOB_s-VREF/2)/(G*Rsh)\n.meas TRAN IB_err_pct PARAM (IB_csa-IB_true)/IB_true*100\n.meas TRAN SOA_hs FIND V(SOA) AT {24/fsw}\n.meas TRAN SOA_pp PP V(SOA) FROM {24/fsw} TO {25/fsw}\n.meas TRAN duty_A FIND V(DA) AT ts\n.meas TRAN Isup_avg AVG -I(Vsup) FROM {15/fsw} TO {25/fsw}\n.meas TRAN Psup PARAM Isup_avg*Vbus\n.meas TRAN Pcopper PARAM 1.5*Rph*Iset**2
TEXT 640 1120 Left 1 ;Notes\n- Ripple: the hold needs only ~1 V line-line, so the active vectors are short;\n  ripple is roughly V_applied x T / L and barely depends on Vbus.  At speed (back-EMF)\n  the active vectors grow and so does the ripple: re-check before closed-loop FOC.\n- The firmware samples once per period at the carrier peak (centre of the low-side window),\n  where the ripple crosses its mean, so IA_csa reads the average current, not the peak.\n- FETs: no layout parasitics or snubbers here (deck 02 covers the edges).\n- CSA model: ideal gain + one pole set from tSET, output clipped to the linear range\n  (0.25 V .. VREF-0.25 V). Offset (+-4 mV = +-67 mA at G=20, 3 mOhm) is calibrated out by\n  the firmware CSA_CAL and is not modelled.\n- Bench: needs a PWM build at 30 V and Iset 5 A: above every approved scope (12 V, 3 A cap,\n  ID modes refused above 15 V). Simulation only until that scope is reviewed.
